<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Shared vocabulary for EPICA ice-core and SISAL speleothem  palaeoclimate Linked Data. Domain extensions import this file."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "geo-lod Core Ontology"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One model's age for one sample. Kept as an assignment and not as a bare property because a sample has as many ages as there are models that reached it, and a consumer has to be able to tell which is which."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Age Assignment"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E13_Attribute_Assignment> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named method for turning dating points into an age at every depth. SISAL v3 carries seven, and the chronology as originally published is an eighth."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Age Model"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMsci/S6_Data_Evaluation> .
