<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/beyondOutermostAgeControlPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True where the sample lies outside the depth span this model's own dating points cover, so its age rests on extrapolation and not on interpolation. Stands next to geolod:extrapolatedBeyondDatingRange, which infers the same thing from a negative age; that inference misfires on a still-growing speleothem, where an age of -50 a is the outermost control point rather than a step past it."@en .
