<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Extension of the geo-lod core ontology for ice-core palaeoclimate records. Covers the drilling site and its boreholes, the core and its sections, the observations of five proxies and the depth-age models their ages rest on."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "EPICA Dome C Ice Core Ontology"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EPICA Dome C Ice Core Ontology"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/epica> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "2.0.0" .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extractedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extractedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a palaeoclimate sample to the sampling location it was extracted from."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extractedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/PalaeoclimateSample> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extractedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "extracted from"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extractedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/SamplingLocation> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extrapolatedBeyondDatingRange> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extrapolatedBeyondDatingRange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True where the model ran past its outermost dating point, which is how an age younger than 1950 arises in a record with no modern control point. Deliberately not expressed through geolod:assignmentStatus: the status says whether geo-lod follows this age, this says whether the model had anything to stand on."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extrapolatedBeyondDatingRange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeAssignment> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extrapolatedBeyondDatingRange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "extrapolated beyond dating range"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/extrapolatedBeyondDatingRange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/fallsWithinStage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/fallsWithinStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Materialised stage membership, following the leading boundary source. The assignment carrying that source and the chronology used is kept alongside as a geolod:MISMembershipAssignment; this property exists so that the common case does not need the join."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/fallsWithinStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/PalaeoclimateObservation> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/fallsWithinStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "falls within stage"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/fallsWithinStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/MarineIsotopeStage> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasAgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasAgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a speleothem sample to one of its age assignments, an age derived from a given age model."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasAgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/SpeleothemSample> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasAgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has age assignment"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasAgeAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeAssignment> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasDrillingCampaign> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasDrillingCampaign> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links an ice-core dataset to the drilling campaign that produced the core."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasDrillingCampaign> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/IceCoreDataset> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasDrillingCampaign> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has drilling campaign"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasDrillingCampaign> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/DrillingCampaign> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasObservation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a resource to an observation made on it."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has observation"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasTimePosition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasTimePosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The age of an observation as a time position, carrying both  the numeric value and the reference system it belongs to. Kept alongside the  plain geolod:ageKaBP literal, which stays queryable without a join."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasTimePosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has time position"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/hasTimePosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TimePosition> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inChronology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inChronology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The depth-age model an assignment depends on. Without it a  derived age or depth cannot be compared with one from another record."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inChronology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in chronology"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inChronology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/Chronology> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inSpeleothem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inSpeleothem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The record a hiatus or a gap belongs to."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inSpeleothem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in speleothem"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/inSpeleothem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/Speleothem> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/interpolationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/interpolationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The method by which a value was obtained between two  measured points. Deliberately not the same property as the smoothing methods:  smoothing rewrites a measured value, interpolation produces one where none  was measured, and a consumer has to be able to tell the two apart."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/interpolationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "interpolation method"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/interpolationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMsci/S6_Data_Evaluation> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isComposite> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True where the record is assembled from several speleothems. A composite has no depth scale of its own - its dating points may carry an age and no depth, and the shapes make that exception explicit."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/Speleothem> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is composite"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isUNESCOWorldHeritage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isUNESCOWorldHeritage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True if the cave belongs to a UNESCO World Heritage Site."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isUNESCOWorldHeritage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/Cave> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isUNESCOWorldHeritage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is UNESCO World Heritage"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/isUNESCOWorldHeritage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/leadingSource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/leadingSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The source geo-lod follows for this entity where the sources disagree."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/leadingSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "leading source"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/leadingSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/DataSource> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/markedBySample> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/markedBySample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The sample row that carries the mark in SISAL. Kept so that the depth in the graph can be traced to the row it came from; the hiatus itself is not that sample."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/markedBySample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "marked by sample"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/markedBySample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/SpeleothemSample> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/materialDated> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/materialDated> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The material that was dated, as recorded in SISAL v3 (free text, unknown when not stated)."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/materialDated> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/strat/AgeControlPoint> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/materialDated> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material dated"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/materialDated> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measuredValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measuredValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The value as measured, before any smoothing, in the unit of the observation's measurement type."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measuredValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/PalaeoclimateObservation> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measuredValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "measured value"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measuredValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measurementType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measurementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The kind of quantity an observation measures (a geolod:MeasurementType), for example methane concentration."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measurementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/PalaeoclimateObservation> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measurementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "measurement type"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/measurementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/MeasurementType> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/mineralogy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/mineralogy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Mineralogy of the speleothem sample (for example calcite or aragonite), as recorded in SISAL v3."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/mineralogy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mineralogy"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/mineralogy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/peakAgeKaBP> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/peakAgeKaBP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Materialised age of the excursion a substage labels."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/peakAgeKaBP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "peak age (ka BP)"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/peakAgeKaBP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/peakAgeKaBP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/ageKaBP> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/polyOrder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/polyOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Polynomial order of a Savitzky-Golay filter."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/polyOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/SavitzkyGolayFilter> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/polyOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "polynomial order"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/polyOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/removedSample> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/removedSample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a sampling event to the sample taken."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/removedSample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "removed sample"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/respectedByAgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/respectedByAgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The models that treated this hiatus as a break instead of interpolating across it. Of the 21 hiatuses in the cut, linear interpolation respected 16 and OxCal none, which is a property of the chronologies and not of the cave."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/respectedByAgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/GrowthHiatus> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/respectedByAgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "respected by age model"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/respectedByAgeModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://w3id.org/geo-lod/AgeModel> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleId> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Identifier of the sample in the SISAL v3 database, kept so that a resource can be traced back to its source table."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SISAL sample id"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
