<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleThickness_mm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Thickness of the sample, in millimetres."@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleThickness_mm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sample thickness (mm)"@en .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/sampleThickness_mm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/screenedForArchaeology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://w3id.org/geo-lod/screenedForArchaeology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True where geo-lod checked this site against the archaeological literature, whatever the outcome. Absence of the property means the site has not been looked at, which is a different statement from a negative result and has to stay distinguishable."@en .
